    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/whitworth/jobs/5481017/assistant-director-advising-and-retention": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Advising and Retention",
      "description": "Job Opportunities | Whitworth University Careers For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Assistant Director, Advising and Retention | Whitworth University Careers page has loaded. Assistant Director, Advising and Retention | Whitworth University Careers page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Whitworth University Careers powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Assistant Director, Advising and Retention Print Apply ﻿ Assistant Director, Advising and Retention Salary $24.61 - $26.06 Hourly Location Whitworth University Campus Job Type Full-Time Staff Division Academic Affairs Department School of Education Opening Date 09/17/2026 FLSA Non-Exempt FTE 1.0 Description Benefits Whitworth University is a residential campus shaped by learning, curiosity, and community life. This role is based on campus and requires consistent, in-person engagement. Position Summary The Assistant Director, Advising and Retention plays a key role in helping graduate students in the School of Education successfully navigate their Whitworth experience from enrollment through completion. This position provides individualized academic advising, monitors student progress, helps students navigate certification and licensure requirements, and connects students with the resources they need to succeed. Working closely with program directors, the Department Chair, Graduate Enrollment Services, and campus partners, the Assistant Director also supports GSE program operations, events, communications, reporting, and continuous improvement. This is a collaborative, student-centered role for someone who enjoys building relationships, solving problems, keeping things moving, and helping students reach their goals. Core Responsibilities Academic Advising, Student Success & Retention | 40% Advise current students regarding program requirements, degree progress, course registration, and completion expectations; develop and maintain individualized degree plans. Assist with transcript evaluations for prospective students and provide program-specific guidance regarding how prior coursework applies to program requirements. Monitor student progress throughout the academic year and establish ongoing communication with students to identify barriers, address concerns, and support timely program completion. Monitor student progress toward licensure, endorsement, and certification requirements and collaborate with the Office of Certification, Career Services, Assessment, and Placement to ensure requirements are understood and addressed before program completion. Coordinate with program directors and appropriate university offices to respond to student concerns and connect students with academic and student support resources. Partner with the Department Chair and program directors to develop and implement proactive student communication and retention strategies. Collaborate with campus partners, including the Registrar, Financial Aid, Student Accounts, Educational Support Services, and Housing, to resolve student needs and support academic success. Maintain accurate and timely records of advising interactions, degree plans, course registration, academic standing, anticipated graduation dates, and other student progress information. Provide regular updates to program directors regarding student progress, advising trends, and emerging student needs. GSE Program Support | 30% Provide project coordination support for Graduate Studies in Education (GSE) programs, ensuring program activities and processes are completed accurately and timely. Coordinate with program directors and appropriate university offices regarding scholarship application and award processes. Track modifications to program plans through university-wide approval processes, such as GECCo, as needed. Coordinate with the International Education Center and International Admissions to support compliance and oversight of Curricular Practical Training for international students. Coordinate with program directors and Student Financial Services to support federally required attendance verification and Regular and Substantive Interaction (RSI) documentation for each term. Assist program directors with collecting, organizing, and maintaining data for annual reporting, including program assessment, strategic enrollment, and program effectiveness activities. Gather and communicate student and alumni feedback and collaborate with program directors and the Department Chair to identify opportunities for program improvement and student success. Participate actively in program-specific, GSE team, and School of Education meetings and contribute to discussions regarding program operations, student needs, and continuous improvement. Maintain current knowledge of and adhere to university-wide and GSE/School of Education policies and procedures, particularly those involving Academic Affairs, Student Financial Services, the Registrar, and other related departments. Event Planning & Support | 15% Coordinate the planning and implementation of GSE program-specific and GSE-wide events, including interviews, orientations, trainings, conferences, institutes, professional development, and partnership events. Manage event logistics, including registration, event webpages, communications, event checklists, guest speaker support, materials, and coordination with campus and external partners. Coordinate event-related budgets, expenditures, and administrative processes in accordance with university policies and established program budgets. Provide staff support at graduate commencement and other major School of Education events as needed. Program Communications | 10% Serve as a program resource to Graduate Enrollment Services (GES), providing accurate and timely information regarding GSE programs, program requirements, certification pathways, and other program-specific questions. Collaborate with GES and GSE program directors to ensure program information communicated to prospective students is accurate, current, and consistent with approved program requirements. Collaborate with GSE staff and program directors to review program websites and identify needed updates to ensure information is accurate and current. Coordinate with GSE staff, program directors, and appropriate campus partners regarding program marketing materials and promotional items, including inventory, ordering, and updates. Provide program information, student accomplishments, and other content to support GSE and School of Education communications, newsletters, social media, and other promotional efforts. Support communication of program changes and updates to GES and other campus partners as appropriate. Other | 5% Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned in support of the mission and operational needs of the School of Education. Qualifications and Core Competencies Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education and relevant professional experience. Three years of professional experience in higher education, adult education, academic advising, student services, program coordination, or a related field. A personal commitment to the Christian faith and to the integration of faith and learning. A commitment to the educational mission of Whitworth University as a Christian liberal arts university affiliated with the Presbyterian Church. Core Competencies Ability to manage a substantial portfolio of students and programs while providing responsive, individualized advising and support across competing priorities and deadlines. Strong organizational skills with the ability to prioritize work, manage schedules and deadlines, maintain accurate documentation, and effectively coordinate multiple projects and responsibilities. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to clearly explain complex academic and program information to students, faculty, staff, and other stakeholders. Demonstrated interpersonal skills and ability to build effective working relationships with students, faculty, staff, campus departments, and external partners. Ability to take initiative, work independently, exercise sound judgment, and identify and address issues while also contributing effectively as a member of a collaborative team. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to interpret data, identify trends, evaluate information, and develop practical solutions to support student and program success. Ability to adapt to changing priorities, policies, processes, and student needs and contribute ideas that improve programs, services, and student experiences. Demonstrated personal integrity, discretion, professionalism, and commitment to maintaining confidentiality and exercising sound judgment in interactions and decision-making. Other Details Schedule Full-time (1.0 FTE) | 12 months | 40 hours per week Whitworth office hours are 8 AM to 4:30 PM Monday – Friday Whitworth University is a Christian liberal arts university. Our shared mission is to provide our diverse students with an education of mind and heart, equipping them to honor God, follow Christ, and serve humanity. We seek candidates who are willing to engage with the university’s mission and integrate their Christian faith into their work. Interested candidates should submit a cover letter, resume, faith statement, and contact information for at least three professional references. A background check and sexual misconduct check will be required of the successful candidate. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain valid work authorization throughout the duration of employment, including those on OPT. Whitworth University does not offer visa sponsorship for this position. You are on this webpage because a position at Whitworth sparked your curiosity. If you find yourself questioning hitting the apply button because you might not meet 100% of the qualifications, we think you should do it! When you click apply and submit an application,  your application is reviewed by a committee of real, living, and breathing human beings who want to understand your background, experience and skills to find ways you relate to the key competencies needed for success in the position. Looking for resources to help with writing a faith statement? Check out our faith statement resource page for more information. Whitworth complies with all federal, state, and local nondiscrimination laws that are applicable to religious nonprofit institutions and does not engage in unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, sexual orientation, sex, or disability. With our Christ-centered commitment to building a diverse and inclusive community, the university encourages applications from populations underrepresented at Whitworth including members of racial/ethnic communities, women, and persons with disabilities. Online applications are stored on a secure site. Only authorized employees and hiring authorities have access to the information submitted. It is important that your application show all the relevant education and experience you possess.  Applications may be rejected if incomplete. At Whitworth University, we are committed to supporting the well-being of our faculty, staff, and their families by offering an extensive benefits package. Eligible employees can enjoy a variety of benefits, including: Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage Employer-matched 403 (b) retirement plan Tuition remission programs available for employees, their spouses, and dependents Life insurance and long-term disability coverage Accrued vacation and sick leave based on full-time equivalency (FTE). All staff accrue 8 hours of sick leave per month and 10 to 20 days of vacation per year, depending on employee category. 2 days of Floating Holiday leave based on full-time equivalency (FTE) Access to an Employee Assistance Program Resources for Christian vocation and calling No cost access to the University Recreation Center (UREC) and the Megan E. Thompson Aquatic Center 15 paid holidays throughout the year To discover more about these offerings, please visit our benefits page . Employer Whitworth University Address 300 W Hawthorne Spokane, Washington, 99251 Phone 5097774872 Website http://www.whitworth.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. Whitworth University Careers Job Opportunities Menu Close Menu Whitworth University Careers Job Opportunities Faculty Openings Staff 