    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/whitworth/jobs/5499180/administrative-coordinator-enrollment-management": {
      "title": "Administrative Coordinator, Enrollment Management",
      "description": "Job Opportunities | Whitworth University Careers For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Administrative Coordinator, Enrollment Management | Whitworth University Careers page has loaded. Administrative Coordinator, Enrollment Management | Whitworth University Careers page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Whitworth University Careers powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Administrative Coordinator, Enrollment Management Print Apply ﻿ Administrative Coordinator, Enrollment Management Salary $20.00 - $20.50 Hourly Location Whitworth University Campus Job Type Full-Time Staff Division Enrollment Services Department Enrollment Management Opening Date 09/29/2026 FLSA Non-Exempt FTE 1.0 Description Benefits Whitworth University is a residential campus shaped by learning, curiosity, and community life. This role is based on campus and requires consistent, in-person engagement. Position Summary The Administrative Coordinator, Enrollment Management provides administrative support to the Vice President for Enrollment Management while serving as a key front-line ambassador for Whitworth University. As the primary administrative coordinator for the Enrollment Management office in Viren House, this role supports the daily operations of a dynamic division that serves prospective and current students. The position coordinates executive and office support functions, oversees telephone coverage and student employees, and helps create a welcoming, organized, and responsive environment for students, families, visitors, and campus partners. Core Responsibilities Vice President & Divisional Administrative Support | 35% Provide administrative support to the Vice President for Enrollment Management, including calendar and appointment coordination, meeting preparation, travel arrangements, expense processing, and purchasing card reconciliation. Schedule and coordinate divisional meetings, retreats, events, and other activities; prepare related materials, correspondence, reports, presentations, and documents. Assist with purchasing, invoices, budget tracking, work orders, reimbursements, and other routine administrative processes. Maintain organized electronic and physical records and handle confidential or sensitive information with appropriate discretion. Support special projects and initiatives of the Vice President and Enrollment Management leadership team. Coordinate communication and information across Enrollment Management departments and with other university offices. Provide general administrative support that contributes to an organized, responsive, and welcoming Enrollment Management office. Admissions Welcome Center & Visitor Experience | 25% Serve as the primary receptionist in the Admissions Welcome Center, warmly and professionally greeting prospective students, families, campus guests, and other visitors. Welcome and check in guests, answer questions, provide directions, and connect visitors with appropriate staff and resources. Partner with the Prospective Student Engagement and Campus Events team to support daily visits, major campus visit programs, and other prospective student activities. Ensure the Welcome Center and associated visitor spaces are organized, professional, and prepared for guests, including coordinating materials, signage, room preparation, and other visit logistics. Develop and maintain knowledge of Whitworth's academic programs, admissions processes, campus resources, and visit opportunities to assist visitors effectively. Anticipate and respond to visitor needs and changing circumstances with flexibility, sound judgment, and a service-oriented approach. Represent Whitworth's mission and values through interactions that help visitors feel known, valued, and welcomed. University Phone & Front-Line Service Coordination | 20% Coordinate the university's main telephone line, providing friendly and accurate assistance and directing inquiries to the appropriate office or individual. Maintain working knowledge of university departments, programs, services, events, and resources, along with current directories and procedures needed to route inquiries accurately. Recruit, train, schedule, and supervise student employees who provide telephone coverage; establish service expectations and provide ongoing coaching, feedback, and support. Ensure appropriate coverage during university business hours, including busy periods, student breaks, and schedule changes. Monitor service quality and recommend improvements to the caller experience and university responsiveness. Serve as a helpful first point of contact for prospective students, families, current students, employees, alumni, and community members. Enrollment Management Operations & Program Support | 15% Provide administrative and project support across the Enrollment Management Division, including Undergraduate Admissions, Enrollment Operations, Prospective Student Engagement and Campus Events, Student Financial Services, Graduate Enrollment Services, and Military & Veteran Resources and Outreach. Support divisional events, programs, meetings, special projects, and periods of significant enrollment activity or major university events. Assist with data entry, information management, mailings, communications, purchasing, supplies, facilities requests, and other operational activities using university systems, including the customer relationship management system. Identify opportunities to improve administrative processes, service, and efficiency within the division. Other Responsibilities | 5% Participate in Enrollment Management and university meetings, activities, and professional development as appropriate. Support university and Enrollment Management events that may occasionally require evening or weekend participation. Perform other related duties and special projects as assigned. Qualifications and Core Competencies Whitworth considers candidates with a wide range of educational backgrounds. We value the skills and knowledge candidates bring to Whitworth, regardless of the paths they have taken to acquire them. One to two years of administrative, customer service, hospitality, office, or related experience; an equivalent combination of education and experience will be considered. Commitment to a welcoming university community in which students, families, colleagues, and visitors are treated with dignity, respect, and care. Demonstrated commitment to exceptional service and creating a welcoming experience for others. A personal commitment to the Christian faith and to the integration of faith and learning. Commitment to the educational mission of Whitworth University as a comprehensive Christian liberal arts university affiliated with the Presbyterian Church. Core Competencies Strong interpersonal, written, verbal, and professional telephone communication skills, with the ability to interact effectively with prospective students, families, employees, and members of the public. Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to manage multiple priorities and remain effective amid frequent interruptions. Sound judgment, discretion, and professionalism when handling confidential or sensitive information. Demonstrated ability to collaborate with a wide variety of people and university departments. Ability to recruit, train, schedule, supervise, and provide direction to student employees. Proficiency with Microsoft 365 and willingness and ability to learn new technology and university systems. Ability to take initiative, anticipate needs, solve routine problems independently, and recognize when issues should be elevated. Willingness and ability to learn about Whitworth University, including its academic programs, services, organizational structure, and resources, to assist visitors and callers effectively. Preferred Qualifications Associate's or bachelor's degree. Experience in higher education, admissions, hospitality, customer service, reception, or an executive or administrative office environment. Experience supervising or providing direction to student or part-time employees. Experience with CRM, scheduling, event management, or similar systems. Other Details Schedule Full-time (1.0 FTE) | 12 months | 40 hours per week Whitworth office hours are 8 a.m. to 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday. Occasional evening or weekend work may be required in support of university or enrollment events. Whitworth University is a Christian liberal arts university. Our shared mission is to provide our diverse students with an education of mind and heart, equipping them to honor God, follow Christ, and serve humanity. We seek candidates who are willing to engage with the university’s mission and integrate their Christian faith into their work. Interested candidates should submit a cover letter, resume, faith statement, and contact information for at least three professional references. A background check and sexual misconduct check will be required of the successful candidate. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain valid work authorization throughout the duration of employment, including those on OPT. Whitworth University does not offer visa sponsorship for this position. You are on this webpage because a position at Whitworth sparked your curiosity. If you find yourself questioning hitting the apply button because you might not meet 100% of the qualifications, we think you should do it! When you click apply and submit an application,  your application is reviewed by a committee of real, living, and breathing human beings who want to understand your background, experience and skills to find ways you relate to the key competencies needed for success in the position. Looking for resources to help with writing a faith statement? Check out our faith statement resource page for more information. Whitworth complies with all federal, state, and local nondiscrimination laws that are applicable to religious nonprofit institutions and does not engage in unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, sexual orientation, sex, or disability. With our Christ-centered commitment to building a diverse and inclusive community, the university encourages applications from populations underrepresented at Whitworth including members of racial/ethnic communities, women, and persons with disabilities. Online applications are stored on a secure site. Only authorized employees and hiring authorities have access to the information submitted. It is important that your application show all the relevant education and experience you possess.  Applications may be rejected if incomplete. At Whitworth University, we are committed to supporting the well-being of our faculty, staff, and their families by offering an extensive benefits package. Eligible employees can enjoy a variety of benefits, including: Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage Employer-matched 403 (b) retirement plan Tuition remission programs available for employees, their spouses, and dependents Life insurance and long-term disability coverage Accrued vacation and sick leave based on full-time equivalency (FTE). All staff accrue 8 hours of sick leave per month and 10 to 20 days of vacation per year, depending on employee category. 2 days of Floating Holiday leave based on full-time equivalency (FTE) Access to an Employee Assistance Program Resources for Christian vocation and calling No cost access to the University Recreation Center (UREC) and the Megan E. Thompson Aquatic Center 15 paid holidays throughout the year To discover more about these offerings, please visit our benefits page . Employer Whitworth University Address 300 W Hawthorne Spokane, Washington, 99251 Phone 5097774872 Website http://www.whitworth.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. Whitworth University Careers Job Opportunities Menu Close Menu Whitworth University Careers Job Opportunities Faculty Openings Staff Openings Help & Support Translate Support Job Application Job Details Applying as: | Support Close Close Cancel Clear SIGN Save We've updated our Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. Please, read and accept changes. Effective date: August 19, 2025 NEOGOV PRIVACY POLICY Contents 1. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. 2. Where We Are a Service Provider. 3. Personal Data We Collect About You and Why. 4. Cookies and Similar Tracking Technologies. 5. Online Analytics and Advertising. 6. Informa